{
    "test_name": "MOB.393_Work_Add_Form",
    "details": {
        "name": "MOB.393_Work_Add_Form",
        "type": "browser",
        "status": "paused",
        "message": "`MOB.393` The **add-form** modal opens and offers its picker.\n- **READ-ONLY BY DESIGN \u2014 do not make it submit again.** It used to add the `Inspection`\n  form for real, and AdHocForm hides forms already attached, so it passed once and then\n  failed forever at *Pick Inspection* (trap 10), keeping all of `MOB.991` red.\n- What it proves: the Forms tab opens, the add modal opens, and the form picker renders\n  with options. What it does NOT prove: that adding one persists.\n- The fill-out flow \u2014 which is the valuable half \u2014 is covered by **MOB.134**, using the\n  `Inspection` form this test attached on its single successful run.",
        "tags": [
            "Mobile",
            "env:dev",
            "Work Order",
            "CRUD",
            "Forms",
            "read-only"
        ],
        "locations": [
            "gcp:us-west2"
        ],
        "config": {
            "assertions": [],
            "config_variables": [
                {
                    "id": "fe7958bf-435f-4932-af8e-0931caab79e7",
                    "name": "MOBDEV",
                    "type": "global"
                }
            ],
            "request": {
                "headers": {},
                "method": "GET",
                "url": "{{ MOBDEV }}"
            },
            "variables": [
